# The program built in C++ by Builder.cpp, compiled and run.
#
# Every other test passes its own .mlir, so this is the one that covers the
# no-input path -- worth keeping, because that is what a bare `hexir` run does.
#
# REQUIRES: runtime, compiler
# RUN: %hexir -emit=hxb -o %t.hxb
# RUN: %hexir-run --quiet %t.hxb | FileCheck %s

# [[3,1],[2,2]] x [[1,5],[5,2]]
# CHECK:      8.000000 17.000000
# CHECK-NEXT: 12.000000 14.000000
